<title>HONDURAS: GM distributor in Honduras accused of tax fraud.</title>
<headline>GM distributor in Honduras accused of tax fraud.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Attorney General's Office of Honduras on Monday accused the local distributor for General Motors of tax fraud in importing vehicles.</p>
<p>Deputy Attorney General Max Santos told reporters that Automotores, which distributes Chevrolet models in this Central American country, evaded paying 10 million lempiras ($789,000) on 232 imported cars.</p>
<p>&quot;The fraud has occured. It was done in complicity with employees in the customs warehouse,&quot; Santos said.</p>
<p>The manager of Automotores, Pami Marinakys, denied the charges. &quot;This is totally false,&quot; she told Reuters.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Palencia, Tegucigalpa bureau, (504) 39 28 85</p>
